# Solve-side tmux canary runner audit

- [ ] Only the preregistered extractor role and frozen non-gold inputs enter the workspace.
- [ ] Start verifies the exact requested POC freeze manifest before launching Devin.
- [ ] `--attempt-id` is mandatory and exactly binds the requested POC ID; no historical default can contaminate receipts.
- [ ] Live and final bundles are children of the approved D-volume solve-vein data root on one device; README hashes and symlink boundaries are checked.
- [ ] The requested profile is `glm-5-2`, high-by-UID, dangerous, no sandbox, one attempt and no retry.
- [ ] The frozen role `AGENTS.md` grants only workspace-local authority even though the CLI approval mode is dangerous/bypass.
- [ ] Status appends pane and health evidence instead of foreground sleeping.
- [ ] Exit sends exactly one recorded `/exit` plus `Enter` intervention.
- [ ] Finalize requires a dead pane; abort preserves the failed bundle and reason.
- [ ] No command connects DB/Redis, launches a Target Solver, or imports absorb-side code.
